contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'execlp', 'Delete the character under the cursor', 'Count the number of lines, words, and characters', 'Finished checking spelling', 'Go one screenful down', 'Go forward one word', 'Toggle appending', 'Go to next block of text', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', 'Use this alternative spell checker', 'speller', 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', 'Invoke the spell checker, if available', 'Search forward for a string or a regular expression', 'Save file without prompting', 'Go to first row in the viewport', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', '0C 40', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', '(%s)       ', 'Show cursor in file browser & help text', '%*zd', 'Edit a replacement', 'spG', 'spelling correction', 'I>K', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', 'Justify the entire file', 'Insert the next keystroke verbatim', 'Search next occurrence backward', 'Start/stop recording a macro', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', ' The following function keys are available in Linter mode:', 'strtok', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', '=== Linter ===', 'a0@', '/lib/ld-linux.so.3', ' The following 