Existing strings in /workspaces/RevEng/string_diffs/nano/positive_strings.txt: 212, {'--nowrap', 'Execute Command Help Text', 'Welcome to nano.  For basic help, type Ctrl+G.', 'Go to line and column number', 'Search Command Help Text', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', '\t\t  %s', '\t`H', 'SPELL', 'If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.', 'Go to the first line of the file', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', ' The following function keys are available in Insert File mode:', 'wait', '$0F', 'Undo the last operation', 'Toggle the use of DOS format', 'execvp', 'Toggle the use of Mac format', '_0E', 'tolower', 'B^K', 'atoi', 'Could not get size of pipe buffer', ' The following function keys are available in Go To Line mode:', '--breaklonglines', 'Write File Help Text', 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", 'Main nano help text', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', 'Switch to the next file buffer', '!0C', '\t0S', 'fpathconf', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Spell Check', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', 'Go back one word', 'Error invoking "spell"', '+0C', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', " This mode allows you to insert the output of a command run by the shell into the current buffer (or into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' (the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'execlp', 'Delete the character under the cursor', 'Count the number of lines, words, and characters', 'Finished checking spelling', 'Go one screenful down', 'Go forward one word', 'Toggle appending', 'Go to next block of text', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', 'Use this alternative spell checker', 'speller', 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', 'Invoke the spell checker, if available', 'Search forward for a string or a regular expression', 'Save file without prompting', 'Go to first row in the viewport', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', '0C 40', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', '(%s)       ', 'Show cursor in file browser & help text', '%*zd', 'Edit a replacement', 'spG', 'spelling correction', 'I>K', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', 'Justify the entire file', 'Insert the next keystroke verbatim', 'Search next occurrence backward', 'Start/stop recording a macro', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', ' The following function keys are available in Linter mode:', 'strtok', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', '=== Linter ===', 'a0@', '/lib/ld-linux.so.3', ' The following function keys are available at this prompt:', '!@ ', 'Close buffer without saving it', 'Push the cursor line to the center, then top, then bottom', 'Go to previous block of text', 'Unindent the current line (or marked lines)', 'Scroll down one line without moving the cursor textually', '70@', ' --disable-utf8', 'Go to the matching bracket', ' Enter the words or characters you would like to search for, and then press Enter.  If there is a match for the text you entered, the screen will be updated to the location of the nearest match for the search string.', 'Switch to the previous file buffer', 'Display the position of the cursor', 'Unfindable word: %s', '0bR', 'Delete the character to the left of the cursor', 'getc_unlocked', 'F12', 'toupper', '#0C', 'Go to last row in the viewport', 'Go one screenful up', 'Error invoking "uniq"', 'Go to previous line', 'Go just beyond end of paragraph; then of next paragraph', '0`F', 'Nothing changed', 'sort', 'Redo the last undone operation', 'Automatically hard-wrap overlong lines', "Don't hard-wrap long lines [default]", '8-A', 'Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.  The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.  Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:', 'Execute a function or an external command', 'Display this help text', '--speller=<program>', 'If you have selected text with the mark and then search to replace, only matches in the selected text will be replaced.', ' The following function keys are available in Search mode:', '--showcursor', 'Indent the current line (or marked lines)', 'Go To Line Help Text', "Program '%s' complained", 'Go to end of current line', '`F ', 'Scroll up one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Pipe the current buffer (or marked region) to the command', ' The previous search string will be shown in brackets after the search prompt.  Hitting Enter without entering any text will perform the previous search.  ', 'A0@', '0PE', 'Center the line where the cursor is', 'M-#', 'Throw away the current line (or marked region)', '--magic', 'Search backward for a string or a regular expression', '=== Replacement ===', ' The following function keys are available in Write File mode:', '_0J', 'Insert File Help Text', ' Type the name that you wish to save the current file as and press Enter to save the file.', 'Toggle backing up of the original file', 'Invoking formatter...', 'Close the current buffer / Exit from nano', 's@-', 'hunspell', ' You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.', 'Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', '--linenumbers', 'Replace a string or a regular expression', 'Toggle prepending', 'Also try magic to determine syntax', 'Paste the contents of cutbuffer at current cursor position', 'Go forward one character', '^?D', 'Invoking spell checker...', ' In this mode, the status bar shows an error message or warning, and the cursor is put at the corresponding position in the file.  With PageUp and PageDown you can switch to earlier and later messages.', 'Go to the last line of the file', 'M-L', '-s <program>', 'ld-linux.so.3', 'JNK', '_0Z', 'Insert a tab at the cursor position (or indent marked lines)', '7@-', '%s\t\t %s %s', 'Suspend the editor (return to the shell)', 'Error invoking "sort"', ' --disable-histories', 'UUU', 'Toggle the use of regular expressions', '$pG', 'Reverse the direction of the search', '2 B', '`0@', 'Do not convert from DOS/Mac format', 'uniq', ' The spell checker checks the spelling of all text in the current file.  When an unknown word is encountered, it is highlighted and a replacement can be edited.  It will then prompt to replace every instance of the given misspelled word in the current file, or, if you have selected text with the mark, in the selected text.', '  C', ' Enter the line number that you wish to go to and hit Enter.  If there are fewer lines of text than the number you entered, you will be brought to the last line of the file.', 'Go to next line', 'A>K', ' --disable-wordcomp', ';p@-', '0@C', 'The bottom two lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.', ' The following function keys are available in Spell Check mode:', 'Buffer has been processed', 'Go to beginning of current line', 'Buffer is empty', 'Cut from the cursor position to the end of the file', 'Go to beginning of paragraph; then of previous paragraph', 'Justify the current paragraph', 'If you need another blank buffer, do not enter any filename, or type in a nonexistent filename at the prompt and press Enter.', 'Toggle the case sensitivity of the search', 'formatting', '%s                ', 'Help', 'Mark text starting from the cursor position', 'Go back one character', 'Next word...', 'Spell Check Help Text', ' G2', '(pg', '0B0<0', 'Run the last recorded macro', 'Search next occurrence forward', "Error invoking '%s'", 'enable/disable', 'Show line numbers in front of the text', 'Cancel the current function'}
