postive strings ['--nowrap', 'Execute Command Help Text', 'Welcome to nano.  For basic help, type Ctrl+G.', 'Go to line and column number', 'Search Command Help Text', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', '\t\t  %s', '\t`H', 'SPELL', 'If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.', 'Go to the first line of the file', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', ' The following function keys are available in Insert File mode:', 'wait', '$0F', 'Undo the last operation', 'Toggle the use of DOS format', 'execvp', 'Toggle the use of Mac format', '_0E', 'tolower', 'B^K', 'atoi', 'Could not get size of pipe buffer', ' The following function keys are available in Go To Line mode:', '--breaklonglines', 'Write File Help Text', 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", 'Main nano help text', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', 'Switch to the next file buffer', '!0C', '\t0S', 'fpathconf', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'Spell Check', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', 'Go back one word', 'Error invoking "spell"', '+0C', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', " This mode allows you to insert the output of a command run by the shell into the current buffer (or into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' (the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'execlp', 'Delete the character under the cursor', 'Count the number of lines, words, and characters', 'Finished checking spelling', 'Go one screenful down', 'Go forward one word', 'Toggle appending', 'Go to next block of text', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', 'Use this alternative spell checker', 'speller', 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', 'Invoke the spell checker, if available', 'Search forward for a string or a regular expression', 'Save file without prompting', 'Go to first row in the viewport', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', '@0C', '0C 40', 'mouseinterval', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', '(%s)       ', 'Show cursor in file browser & help text', '%*zd', 'Edit a replacement', 'spG', 'spelling correction', 'I>K', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', 'Justify the entire file', 'Insert the next keystroke verbatim', 'Search next occurrence backward', 'Start/stop recording a macro', '--mouse', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', ' The following function keys are available in Linter mode:', 'strtok', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', '=== Linter ===', 'a0@', '/lib/ld-linux.so.3', ' The following function keys are available at this